      "diagnostic": "Domain: nominal-categories / definiteness. GB020=1 lands at rank 25 (sim=0.9511) — the signal is present but the WALS 37A language profile is dominated by a head-initial areal cluster (ranks 1–24 are all word-order and adposition features such as GB074=1, GB075=0, GB133=0), which drowns out the definiteness correspondence. The mismatch arises because definiteness marking co-occurs with head-initial word order areally (e.g. European languages), so the language-profile similarity peak falls on word-order features, not on Grambank's binary definiteness feature."
